{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions","id":1518658,"title":"Kuei Jin questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-23T12:44:24-07:00","id":1518658,"title":"Kuei Jin questions","content":"Writing here because Kuei-Jin topics seem to be under the Vampire umbrella, if it is better to go to the main forum, let me know and I will repost there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Devil-Tigers have a level 7 ritel (<b>memorial to the merciless ministers</b>) that as part of the process includes a voluntary reduction on the P\u2019o rating. My questions are:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can a non Devil Tiger participate? Text says Devil Tigers, but lots of Kuei Jin from different Dharmas would be to be willing to reduce their P\u2019o.</li> <li>Can you sacrifice more than one dot?</li> <li>What stops a Ritualist (from any non Devil Dharma) from creating a similar rite to lower the P\u2019o? It would be a great boon for those that have issues controlling their urges, and it would make easier to fight negative soul states, to grow in Dharma, etc.</li> </ol>Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T17:49:33-07:00","id":1518670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions#post1518658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writing here because Kuei-Jin topics seem to be under the Vampire umbrella, if it is better to go to the main forum, let me know and I will repost there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Devil-Tigers have a level 7 ritel (<b>memorial to the merciless ministers</b>) that as part of the process includes a voluntary reduction on the P\u2019o rating. My questions are:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can a non Devil Tiger participate? Text says Devil Tigers, but lots of Kuei Jin from different Dharmas would be to be willing to reduce their P\u2019o.</li> <li>Can you sacrifice more than one dot?</li> <li>What stops a Ritualist (from any non Devil Dharma) from creating a similar rite to lower the P\u2019o? It would be a great boon for those that have issues controlling their urges, and it would make easier to fight negative soul states, to grow in Dharma, etc.</li> </ol>Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no to the first point. It only says Devil Tigers so I would say that only Devil Tigers could do it. As for point two, I'd say you could but given that you're offering up a permanent dot of P'o I wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Point three... you could but honestly I wouldn't as we're talking about a ritual that requires sacrificing P'o for. The sacrifice is important and if you're not offering up something that matters to you than it's not really a sacrifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T21:56:13-07:00","id":1518679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions?p=1518670#post1518670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say no to the first point. It only says Devil Tigers so I would say that only Devil Tigers could do it. As for point two, I'd say you could but given that you're offering up a permanent dot of P'o I wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Point three... you could but honestly I wouldn't as we're talking about a ritual that requires sacrificing P'o for. The sacrifice is important and if you're not offering up something that matters to you than it's not really a sacrifice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have another question, if you are a low level Devil Tiger, you can participate (Even if your participation makes the rite more likely to fail)... What happens if you are a low level Devil Tiger, and sacriice all your P\u00b4o?<br /> <br /> Literally, 0 P\u00b4o, what would that make you? The perfect Resplendent Crane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T23:25:50-07:00","id":1518682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions?p=1518679#post1518679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer...<br /> <br /> I have another question, if you are a low level Devil Tiger, you can participate (Even if your participation makes the rite more likely to fail)... What happens if you are a low level Devil Tiger, and sacriice all your P\u00b4o?<br /> <br /> Literally, 0 P\u00b4o, what would that make you? The perfect Resplendent Crane?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would kill you. P'o is what animates you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T00:14:52-07:00","id":1518686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions#post1518658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.Can a non Devil Tiger participate? Text says Devil Tigers, but lots of Kuei Jin from different Dharmas would be to be willing to reduce their P\u2019o</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is a Devil Tiger Rite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And it is not for reducing the P'o<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions#post1518658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.Can you sacrifice more than one dot?.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> As per the Ritual, before sending it, the ritualist must make their chop-mark on the document, and this causes him to permanently lose a point of P'o as he attaches a bit of his wickedness to the document to lend it credence<br /> Other Devil Tigers may make their chop-marks on the rite to show their support for the measure (also losing a point of permanent P'o in the process), but the marks of vampires below Dharma 6 are unlikely to do much in the way of helping the document gain celestial attention, and those of disciples are actively injurious to the memorial's chances. If the ministers of Heaven wanted to hear what the Running Monkeys have to say, they'd ask.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions#post1518658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3.What stops a Ritualist (from any non Devil Dharma) from creating a similar rite to lower the P\u2019o? It would be a great boon for those that have issues controlling their urges, and it would make easier to fight negative soul states, to grow in Dharma, etc.Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kuei-Jin are not Cainites<br /> They think differently<br /> The Ritual of <b>Memorial to the Merciless Ministers</b>\u200b (Blood &amp; Silk - Pg. 98) is not about the P'o<br /> This rite allows a Devil-Tiger mandarin to send a memorial to Heaven, where it is received by the ministers who deal with such matters as woe, punishment, pestilence and pain. This document, essentially a formal petition, is signed by the Devil-Tiger who wrote it<br /> If the ministers of Heaven agree with the recommendations of the memorial, they may cause the request to be fulfilled. If they are disinterested in the matter, ordered to do otherwise by their superiors, if the matter is beyond their purview or if the target has a powerful horoscope or allies in Heaven or the Yomi Realms, they may be forced to simply ignore the memorial. If the request is presumptuous or awkwardly phrased, the ministers (who are touchy at the best of times) may choose to visit Heaven's wrath on those who presented the memorial, as a lesson that the ministries of punishment and woe are not to be invoked lightly.<br /> This rite is used only in the most critical of circumstances - when a greater <i>akuma</i> is abroad in the land and cannot be put down by the usual means, when a great dragon nest has been destroyed or when a terrible sinner must be subjected to a punishment beyond the capabilities of even the Wan Kuei.<br /> Heaven ceases to acknowledge these memorials of woe with the ending of the Fourth Age.<br /> <br /> The Ritual is something very rare and very sacred thing (and since the end of the Fourth Age - according to scholars, the Fourth Age begins approximately around 900 BCE and ends around 1250-1349 CE (according to the counting of the Kuei-jin) it became basically useless)<br /> Yes, in the past ~2200 years the Heavens not answered the petitions... still porpbably some Devil-Tigers tried to write to them - or not<br /> After all, the whole Devil-Tiger Dharma is about becoming better Devils and the Fifth and Sixth Age is their final test to see they are worthy or not to replace the incompetent Demons and Yama Kings...<br /> Like the goddess Tien Mu, Devil-Tigers are the lightning that illuminates the wicked; like Le Kung, they are the thunderbolt, which strikes down sinners. The Sixth Age, so they say, will be the brightest strike, the flash that will burn a wicked creation to ashes. Like the lightning, the Devil-Tigers will fade when their task is done, and a new, wiser creation will rise from the embers of the old.<br /> <br /> Other Dharmas traditions are not really with the Celestial Bureaucracy and the Ministers of Heaven. What would a Trashing Dragon or a Crane or a Hollow Reed\u200b would wrote or ask? A Bone Flower?<br /> And again, it never ment to be a P'o reducation ceremony, the P'o loss is a side effect, the chop-mark on the document represenzs the Devil-Tiger, the very essence of the Wrtier<br /> A Trashing Dragon, a Bone Flower, a Crane or a Hollow Reed would use a chop-mark with their own essence and that is not the P'o \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions#post1518658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> \u200bLiterally, 0 P\u00b4o, what would that make you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead<br /> Losing your Hun or P'o completly would be losing a part of yourself<br /> The P\u2019o is the \u201clower soul\u201d that awakened in Yomi - brutal, cruel, animalistic. It was the strength of the P\u2019o that allowed the Kuei-Jin to claw their way out of hell.<br /> You will not survive the &quot;loss&quot; of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-24-2023, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T06:57:25-07:00","id":1518699,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar420_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"420\" data-vbnamecard=\"420\">AkatsukiLeader13</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> <br /> <br /> Thanks for reading and replying to my questions.<br /> <br /> A final question, besides the Level 7 rites to create an Ancestor, is there any other rite that provides a permanent benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T07:47:01-07:00","id":1518700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions?p=1518699#post1518699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar420_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"420\" data-vbnamecard=\"420\">AkatsukiLeader13</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a><br /> <br /> Thanks for reading and replying to my questions.<br /> <br /> A final question, besides the Level 7 rites to create an Ancestor, is there any other rite that provides a permanent benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of the top of my head, there is the bakemono rite and the inauspicious object rites. There's bound to be more as the rites in KotE are much more similar to rites in Werewolf than the rituals for Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T07:47:07-07:00","id":1518701,"title":"","content":"Happy to help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As for your question, well.... define &quot;permanent benefit&quot; please<br /> And maybe if specifically want them to use for your character, your Dharma... lots of rites are Dharma-tied<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T07:57:20-07:00","id":1518702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions?p=1518701#post1518701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happy to help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As for your question, well.... define &quot;permanent benefit&quot; please<br /> And maybe if specifically want them to use for your character, your Dharma... lots of rites are Dharma-tied<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Crowning</b><b> the Ancestor</b>, <b>Naming the Ancestor </b>and<b> Welcoming the Penangallan</b>, all grant extra Chi storage, and other benefits that persist as long as the recipient exists and it is not transformed into <i>akuma</i>.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if the rite is Dharma tied, I just want to be aware of its existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  spacing 07-24-2023, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T08:51:42-07:00","id":1518705,"title":"","content":"well...<br /> <br /> <b>Purifications of Rice and Garlic (Level 6 Rite)</b><br /> Through the use of this powerful and closely guarded rite, a Resplendent Crane mandarin may, for a time, become truly holy. Though this state is fragile, it is blessed creatures of wickedness cannot stand against the vampire, and the Crane's touch causes them grave pain. It is said that those in this state who can meet the Eye of Heaven while retaining their composure ascend directly to Heaven. Of course, there is no real evidence of this. With the turning of the Age, this ritual becomes more and more difficult, until it finally ceases to function in the 1700s.<br /> <b>System:</b> The Crane must have her internal organs removed, save for the heart, diaphragm and lungs. Doing this according to the proper ritual forms requires at least 10 cumulative successes on an Intelligence + Medicine check (difficulty 8). One roll is permitted per hour, and the process must be completed by sunrise. Obviously, the vampire cannot do this herself.<br /> In place of the absent internal organs, the vampire's body is stuffed with white rice fumigated in the most expensive of incenses and garlic cloves upon which have been carved prayers to the buddhas and the ministers of Heaven. This process causes the vampire to take three health levels of unsoakable lethal damage that cannot be healed until the vampire's insides are allowed to return to their normal configuration. Carving the garlic requires 50 successes on a Dexterity + Crafts (Carving) roll (difficulty 8), though assistants can be employed, provided they are properly purified during the work.<br /> The vampire must then stay awake, meditating, all through the daylight hours, This requires three Stamina + Meditation rolls: One at difficulty 7, one at difficulty 8 and one at difficulty 9. If all three rolls succeed, the player must make a test just as if the character had reached an auspicious occasion (see <b>Kindred of the East</b>, p. 52-53). If the P'o succeeds, the vampire immediately dies the Little Death from accumulated bodily and spiritual trauma and experiences a concurrent act of blindness. It is traditional to burn the corpse after such failures.<br /> If the vampire succeeds in the Dharma roll, she immediately gains a form of True Faith, The player may roll a number of dice equal to half the vampire's Dharma (round up) to repel wicked creatures as if the vampire had the first level of Western True Faith (as described in <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>, p. 272). The vampire need not use a holy symbol to repel unrighteous beings, though she must pray, gesture or otherwise indicate her displeasure. The vampire's touch also causes one level of aggravated damage to any unrighteous being, in addition to any normal hand-to-hand damage that might apply. Obviously, the vampire's Faith does not affect herself.<br /> This effect lasts until the player fails a soul state roll. While in this state, the vampire cannot perform internal alchemy (as he has no internal organs) and so can only feed by breath or osmosis. In fact, imbibing anything at all is impossible, for the vampire has no stomach. Also while in this state, the vampire cannot spend or gain Demon Chi.<br /> <br /> Blood &amp; Silk - Page 99-100<br /> <br /> <b>The Breathing Mask (Level 7 Rite)</b><br /> It is the greatest desire of the Thrashing Dragons that they return to life. By means of this rite, elder Thrashing Dragons can (to a limited extent) live again. Through great ritual preparation, the Thrashing Dragon can walk in sunlight and experience drugs, sex and alcohol as a normal living human would.<br /> The downsides are the price and the incredibly addictive character of the process. Some of the materials for the rite can be gathered only in the Yang World and the Yomi Realms, and other components such as rhinoceros horn, which must be bought from Silk Road merchants, who carry them from the other side of the world. The cost of even a few doses is enough to leave the purses of even the richest mandarins flat. Even those who can afford it soon cannot because having tasted the breath of life once, there are few indeed who can say no to a second taste and a third and so on. Just as among those who eat the Chi of the <i>hsien</i>, hundreds of years of enlightenment can come crashing down in a few short months of addiction.<br /> The existence of this rite is well known among Thrashing Dragons, at least in rumor. Those elders who know it are unwilling to teach it to those not wise enough to use it as an instruction toward enlightenment and not as a crutch to avoid it. Indeed, many elders refuse to use the rite at all and assiduously conceal their possession of it. The frantic attempts of younger mandarins to obtain this rite, ostensibly for the purposes of enlightenment, are often painful to behold, and this single rite has probably caused more woe to the Dharma than all others combined.<br /> <b>System:</b> Unlike many other rites, this rite can be performed on a Wan Kuei by another vampire or by a Wan Kuei on herself. The subject must be permanently Yang-imbalanced for this rite to work, and the ritualist must have the Science and Occult Knowledges of at least 4 each to perform the complex process of mixing the various ingredients necessary for the potion. This requires an Intelligence + Rituals roll (difficulty 8). The ingredients must be drunk at the next sunrise, and the effects last from sunrise to sunset.<br /> While the rite is in effect, the vampire is alive again. She cannot use Disciplines, cannot spend Chi, does not have access to her innate powers and cannot soak lethal damage. The P'o still whispers in her ear, and she is still subject to shadow soul (although the Hun enjoys a -1 difficulty bonus), but she is immune to fire and wave soul. For the most part, she is a normal mortal. If killed, she suffers the Little Death, regardless of the Cause. Vampires who have been exposed to the rite must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 9) to not attempt to get further access to the Breathing Mask.<br /> <br /> Blood &amp; Silk - Page 103-104<br /> <br /> <b>Embracing the True Death (Level 7 Rite)</b><br /> The ultimate death rite of the Dark Jade Lover is practically a legend among the followers of the Thousand Whispers, undertaken only by those ready to become bodhisattvas. It involves the complete destruction of the body, freeing the soul to wander in the spirit worlds rather than being cast into oblivion - to look death in the eye and to embrace it like an ally, a lover, to welcome it and let go of everything else. Only the most enlightened Kuei-jin can perform this rite successfully; it is very rare in the Fifth Age.<br /> The vampire chooses a place and time for the rite and usually invites fellow wu members and local mandarins to attend. The Kuei-jin faces Final Death in whatever manner he desires, usually by Facing the Eye of Heaven, although self-immolation is popular, particularly among the Kuei-jin of the Golden Courts, and <i>seppuku</i> is common for the <i>gaki</i> of Nippon. After meeting Final Death, the vampire's body turns to dust and scatters on the wind. If the rite is successful, the Kuei-jin's soul enters the spirit worlds and travels there. If not, the vampire is truly dead and gone forever.<br /> There is no way of knowing how long the Kuei-jin's spirit will travel in the spirit worlds - years at least, often a mortal lifetime or more. During that time, the Kuei-jin communes with the shen of the spirit worlds, gaining wisdom and instruction. The Kuei-jin is not aware of the years passing in the Middle Kingdom, but when the spirit is ready, he returns to the physical plane. The dust that made up his body swirls up on the wind, and the Kuei-jin reappears, reborn out of nothingness.<br /> <b>System:</b> Roll the character's Dharma rating against a difficulty of 9. Failure means the character suffers Final Death and is destroyed. Success allows the enlightened spirit to pass on into the spirit worlds. The time and place of the bodhisattva's resurrection is entirely up to the Storyteller.<br /> The Wise Centipede automatically gains one point in his Dharma from the experience and appears completely healed of any damage, with full Chi scores of all types. If desired, the character can re-allocate his permanent Yin and Yang to balance those virtues, if they are not already. The vampire returns in shadow soul and remains there for a full night.<br /> <br /> Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers - Page 59-60<br /> <br /> These are powerfull ones by their own right<br /> But I think the best ones are the &quot;little ones&quot; like <b>Harmonious Shielding of the Guarded Home, </b> <b>Construct the Dragon-Bone Prison, </b> <b>Inauspicious Object, </b> <b>Reflecting the Inner Face, </b> <b>Rite of the Gracious Courier</b> or<b>Stroking the Demon's Fury </b><br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-25-2023, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T19:42:32-07:00","id":1518734,"title":"","content":"Generally if it's in a specific splatbook, which I assume is a Dharma Book, that ability or whatever is typically exclusive unless stated otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T00:32:44-07:00","id":1518741,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, the complet rite- list is:<br /> <br /> <b>Level 0 Rites</b><br /> Conciliatory Doorway Ritual [Heresies of the Way p.101]<br /> <br /> <b>Level One Rites:</b><br /> Trace the Dragon's Blood [Kindred of the East p.127]<br /> Ebbrace the Spirit's Change [Kindred of the East p.130]<br /> Harmonious Shielding of the Guarded Home [Kindred of the East p.131]<br /> Eating the Scorpion [Heresies of the Way p.127]<br /> Greeting the Sun [Dharma Book: Thrashing Dragons p.55]<br /> Prayer for Taking Life [Dharma Book: Thrashing Dragons p.55]<br /> Ritual for Giving Birth [Dharma Book: Thrashing Dragons p.56]<br /> The Ritual of Thousand Cuts [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.57]<br /> The Ashes of the Phoenix [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.57]<br /> The Gentle Repose [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.57]<br /> Center the Demon [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.58]<br /> Rite of the Gracious Courtier [Shadow War p.96]<br /> Blood Preservation [Blood &amp; Silk p.96]<br /> Speak Thrugh the Tongue of the Dragon [Wind from the East p.72]<br /> Sense the Ger [Wind from the East p.72]<br /> <br /> <b>Level Two Rites:</b><br /> Behold The Spirits\u2019 Doorway [Kindred of the East p.127]<br /> The Way of the Lone Walker [Kindred of the East p.129]<br /> Taking the Left-Hand Path [Kindred of the East p.129]<br /> The Mark of Judgment [Dharma Book: Resplendent Cranes p.64]<br /> Savage Joss [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.52]<br /> Ebon Warding [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.56]<br /> Harmony with Night [Dharma Book: Bone Flowers p.61]<br /> Walk the Spirit Path [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.54]<br /> The Folding Lotus [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.55]<br /> Ritual of Guarded Alliance [Heresies of the Way p.102]<br /> Tithing to the Ancestor [Heresies of the Way p.24]<br /> Branding the Criminal [Blood &amp; Silk p.98]<br /> Bindig Goods [Blood &amp; Silk p.96]<br /> Dream of the Suffocating Cat [Blood &amp; Silk p.97]<br /> Sensing the Earth's Sicness [Blood &amp; Silk p.102]<br /> <br /> <b>Level Three Rites:</b><br /> Imbuing the Jade [Kindred of the East p.128]<br /> Construct the Dragon Bone Prison [Kindred of the East p.130]<br /> Asserting the Heavenly Priviliage of Yang Demon Command [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.53]<br /> The Deceptive Jade Chains of Yin Demon Command [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.53]<br /> The Black Silken Pouch [Dharma Book: Bone Flowers p.62]<br /> Donning the Flawless Mask [Dharma Book: Bone Flowers p.62]<br /> Assume the Greater Mask [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.55]<br /> The Scarlet Silk Leash of Yang Spirit Binding [Dharma Book: Thrashing Dragons p.56]<br /> Donning the Necklace of Skulls [Dharma Book: Thrashing Dragons p.57]<br /> Wear the Lesser Mask [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.56]<br /> The Earth's Embrace [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.59]<br /> The Voice Which Comples Truth [Dharma Book: Resplendent Cranes p.64]<br /> Reflecting the Inner Face [Shadow War p.97]<br /> The Ritual of the Black Peony [1000 Hells p.104]<br /> The Rite of Renunciation [1000 Hells p.111]<br /> Stroking the Demon's Fury [Blood &amp; Silk p.96]<br /> Facing the Dynastic Way [Blood &amp; Silk p.125]<br /> Encircle [Wind from the East p.72]<br /> Strength of the Herd [Wind from the East p.73]<br /> Inquisition of the Prying Masitrate [Blood &amp; Silk p.99]<br /> Bone-Oil Kiss [Blood &amp; Silk p.100]<br /> The Ritual of the Invisible Mask [Blood &amp; Silk p.101]<br /> Rite of Beseeching Remembrance [Heresies of the Way p.102]<br /> Mists of the Lotus [Heresies of the Way p.24]<br /> <br /> <b>Level Four Rites:</b><br /> Cloak the Dragon's Passage [Kindred of the East p.128]<br /> Rite of Supplication [Kindred of the East p.129]<br /> Restoring The Dharmic Balance [Kindred of the East p.130]<br /> Speak with Local Beasts [Blood &amp; Silk p.102]<br /> Memories of Torments Unexperianced [Blood &amp; Silk p.97]<br /> Commune with Tengri [Wind from the East p.73]<br /> Commune with Itugen [Wind from the East p.74]<br /> The Pact of Ebony and Scarlet [1000 Hells p.113]<br /> Inauspicious Object [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.54]<br /> Bokemono Rite [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.54]<br /> Beconing the Unrighteous Spirit [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.56]<br /> Honor the Second Breath [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.56]<br /> The Thousand-Eyes Sorcerer [Dharma Book: Thrashing Dragons p.57]<br /> Fabrication of the Elemental Instrument [Dharma Book: Thrashing Dragons p.58]<br /> Reading the Leaves of Wisdom [Blood &amp; Silk p.100]<br /> Shroud Over Death [Heresies of the Way p.24]<br /> Strengthening the Crab's Shell Rite [Heresies of the Way p.103]<br /> <br /> <b>Level Five Rites:</b><br /> Creating The Rivergate [Kindred of the East p.129]<br /> Shitting Down the Dragon's Neck [Heresies of the Way p.107]<br /> Digesting the Feast [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.57]<br /> Gracious Acceptance of the Most Revered Lotus Blossom Gift [Dharma Book: Bone Flowers p.62]<br /> Wisdom of the Spirit Ways [Blood &amp; Silk p.101]<br /> Gather the Broken Mask [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.56]<br /> Embracing the Little Demon [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.59]<br /> <br /> <b>Level Six Rites:</b><br /> Purifications of Rice and Garlic [Blood &amp; Silk p.99]<br /> Ritual of Heavenly Defilement [Dharma Book: Devil-Tigers p.56]<br /> Loose the Wandering Spirit [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.54]<br /> The Righteous Hunt [Blood &amp; Silk p.100]<br /> <br /> <b>Level Seven Rites:</b><br /> Reeds in the Cycle of Seasons [Blood &amp; Silk p.101]<br /> The Breathing Mask [Blood &amp; Silk p.103]<br /> Memorial to the Merciless Ministers [Blood &amp; Silk p.98]<br /> Embracing the True Death [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.59]<br /> Crowning the Ancestor [Blood &amp; Silk p.97]<br /> Naming the Ancestor [Dharma Book: Resplendent Cranes p.65]<br /> Welcoming the Penangallan [Dharma Book: Thousand Whispers p.59]<br /> <br /> <b>Level Eight Rite:</b><br /> The Inauspicious Gate [Dharma Book: Bone Flowers p.63]<br /> <br /> <br /> For some reason I have in my notes some rites I simply coudln't find where are those from, so they are probably home made stuff for one of my chronicles, so I won't post theme here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T00:54:00-07:00","id":1518743,"title":"","content":"Per the Bone Flower Dharmabook, it's also possible to crib Necromancy rituals from Kindred, so long as your Rituals is really high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T17:00:02-07:00","id":1518792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions?p=1518743#post1518743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the Bone Flower Dharmabook, it's also possible to crib Necromancy rituals from Kindred, so long as your Rituals is really high.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it any Kindred with Necromancy that can be targetted by this, or is it mainly in regard Kindred with Necromancy as an in-Clan Discipline ? <br /> <br /> Just wandering about this capability of the Song of Shadows Vampires. They do not seem to me as a Dharma that would steal from or exploit just any other Vampire or Kindred.<br /> The Song of Shadows is a Dharma that insists on a focus on being well defined, calm, and reasonable. With these traits, concepts, attributes, and qualities also comes preference towards clear precautions, limits, and borders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T17:48:24-07:00","id":1518796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions?p=1518792#post1518792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it any Kindred with Necromancy that can be targetted by this, or is it mainly in regard Kindred with Necromancy as an in-Clan Discipline ?<br /> <br /> Just wandering about this capability of the Song of Shadows Vampires. They do not seem to me as a Dharma that would steal from or exploit just any other Vampire or Kindred.<br /> The Song of Shadows is a Dharma that insists on a focus on being well defined, calm, and reasonable. With these traits, concepts, attributes, and qualities also comes preference towards clear precautions, limits, and borders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back on the sidebar (pg 35), it takes Occult 3 and Rituals 4, and it's only basic Necromancy rituals, so presumably not alternate paths. You also have to be Yin-aspected. Finally, Hungry Dead authorities don't like their own using adapted rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T21:55:47-07:00","id":1518810,"title":"","content":"Indeed<br /> And after Encoh's destruction, group of Nagaraja fled to Korea and was granted protection by the Green Court (well know for its Jade and Jade Artifacts, merchants and necromancers - and to be neutral ground between the Quincunx, the Kuei-Jin Courts of China and the Kuei-Jin Ujis, the Houses of the Gaki of Japan) provided that they would never sire... AND share everything they know about the Yin World and their/western Necromancy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T22:14:41-07:00","id":1518811,"title":"","content":"Afraid to edit, so double post...<br /> On Blood &amp; Silk p. 158 there is a &quot;gossip&quot;, not a 100% fact, just &quot;rumors&quot; about the Salubri, the spawns of Zao-Lat and about their potential to awaken their P'o and start their Dharmic journey<br /> It have a lot of ground actually; aside the whole Saulot is two, the White Worm, his P'o and the one, his Hun that is wandering around, and his Devil-Tigerish behavior and mentality when he created the Baali, <i>Chi</i>'<i>iu Muh </i>is the key here, what Saulot/Zao-Lat &quot;have stolen&quot; and refined in to a signiture discipline is almost the same-version of the Wan Kuei Discipline after all\u200b to the point, the Watcher Valeren in Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition have the fifth level of power called <b>Soul's Breath - </b>Subsist on mortals' breaths instead of blood, or steal blood and power from other supernatural creatures through their breath<br /> Not as effective as the Dharmic &quot;benefit&quot;, but still<br /> Such a stransformed Salubri probably would retain their knowledge about rituals too\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T07:10:13-07:00","id":1518929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions?p=1518792#post1518792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it any Kindred with Necromancy that can be targetted by this, or is it mainly in regard Kindred with Necromancy as an in-Clan Discipline ?<br /> <br /> Just wandering about this capability of the Song of Shadows Vampires. They do not seem to me as a Dharma that would steal from or exploit just any other Vampire or Kindred.<br /> The Song of Shadows is a Dharma that insists on a focus on being well defined, calm, and reasonable. With these traits, concepts, attributes, and qualities also comes preference towards clear precautions, limits, and borders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like any of the Dharmas they can be calm, well defined and reasonable killers and thieves, the Song of Shadows have well known assassin sects and WU within their courts.<br /> <br /> Plus they are Lore Keepers so acquistion of forbidden knowledge and rituals are well within their domain, they are also noted to regard the Giovanni with disgust due to their lack of civility and abuse of the First tenet, so studying these abhorent creatures and their powers is prudent (and probably why they did so in the beginning).<br /> <br /> As its mentioned as an option there are Song of Shadow Hungry Dead who do actively acquire necromancy (amongst other things), they'll just be more codified and civil about the whole affair.<br /> However its undoubtly viewed as a corrupt power and a path to the Yama Kings so on the surface of things discouraged by the majority and certainly most Ancestors.<br /> <br /> On more basic terms there will also be Bone Flowers who deviate from the path and easy power, if there weren't then the Hungry Dead wouldn't be susceptible to becoming Akuma or addiction to feeding from the Hsien, I can imagine their are individuals who relish the power of enslaving the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T07:13:14-07:00","id":1518930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518658-kuei-jin-questions?p=1518792#post1518792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it any Kindred with Necromancy that can be targetted by this, or is it mainly in regard Kindred with Necromancy as an in-Clan Discipline ?<br /> <br /> Just wandering about this capability of the Song of Shadows Vampires. They do not seem to me as a Dharma that would steal from or exploit just any other Vampire or Kindred.<br /> The Song of Shadows is a Dharma that insists on a focus on being well defined, calm, and reasonable. With these traits, concepts, attributes, and qualities also comes preference towards clear precautions, limits, and borders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like any of the Dharmas they can be calm, well defined and reasonable killers and thieves, the Song of Shadows have well known assassin sects and WU within their courts, plus they are Lore Keepers so acquistion of forbidden knowledge and rituals are well within their domain.<br /> <br /> They are also noted to regard the Giovanni with disgust due to their lack of civility and abuse of the First tenet, so studying these abhorent creatures and their powers is prudent (and probably why they did so in the beginning).<br /> <br /> As its mentioned as an option there are Song of Shadow Hungry Dead who do actively acquire necromancy (amongst other things), they'll just be more codified and civil about the whole affair.<br /> However its undoubtly viewed by most as a clumsy, indelicate and even corrupt power and potentially a path to the Yama Kings, so on the surface of things discouraged by the majority and certainly most Ancestors.<br /> <br /> On more basic terms there will also be Bone Flowers who deviate from the path and seek easy power, if there weren't, then the Hungry Dead wouldn't be susceptible to becoming Akuma or addiction to feeding from the Hsien, I can imagine their are individuals who relish the power of enslaving the dead.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T08:59:12-07:00","id":1520454,"title":"","content":"Another set of questions (I did ask on the general forum <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1338019-kote-ancestor-rites\">once</a>, but this is the Vampire place) about ancestor rites (rites that crown a Kuei-Jin as an Ancestor that is):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The rites <b><i>Naming the Ancestor</i></b> (Resplendent Cranes p. 65) and <i>W<b>elcoming the Penangallan </b></i>(Thrashing Dragons p. 59) substitute the older rite <i><b>Crowning the Ancestor</b> </i>(Blood and Silk p. 97), so what happened with that rite? Does no longer work or people have forgotten it?</li> <li>If a rite no longer works (probable case with <b><i>Crowning the Ancestor</i></b>) those under its effect lose them?</li> <li>Can a Kuei-Jin be under the effect of two ancestor rites (<b><i>Crowning the Ancestor</i></b> and<b> <i>Welcoming the Penangallan</i></b>, or <b><i>Naming the Ancestor</i></b> and <b><i>Welcoming the Penangallan</i></b>)? If so, do the effects overlap or are cumulative?</li> </ol>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T16:18:49-07:00","id":1520556,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that Blood and Silk takes place in the Fourth Age while the modern era is the Fifth Age and that in that transition between ages things changed in the world. If I remember right the Chi of the world became weaker which in turn weakened the Wan Kuei and their abilities. As a result the Disciplines and Rites of the Wan Kuei diminished over time.<br /> <br /> Personally I would say that the older Rite would be more powerful and dominant over their modern equivalents so that would always take precedence. As for the two modern ones, it's unlikely that they would be in conflict like that as the Penangallan is a regional one and tied to the Wan Kuei of that region who do not follow the same practices as other Wan Kuei who would use the other Rite.<br /> <br /> As for the old Rite losing it's power and the effects no longer working, I don't know. We don't really know what happened with the changing of the Ages and the decline in their power as we didn't see it and don't know all the effects that had. So it's possible that the effects of the original diminished or ceased to exist. It's also possible that the effects of the original Rite remained but that no one could use that Rite anymore and as Ancestors died or advanced their Dharma to Bodhisattva and beyond, resulting in those Wan Kuei becoming rarer and rarer until none remained in the modern age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}